    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello everyone!\r\n\r\nI'm a Neovim newbie, so this might be a big factor. But personally I don't understand why `autoread` config by default is set to `false`. After setting up the `mini.sessions` with default config I've realized that my session is saved automatically, but for some reason not loaded automatically at the start of nvim. I've spent couple of hours trying to figure out why this was happening. Only then I've realized that `autoread` must be explicitly set to `true`\r\n\r\nPartially I blame my own blindness - it is mentioned in the [default-config ](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-sessions.md#default-config) at which I've looked at least a couple of times. But partially my expectation was that sessions manager should automatically save AND load sessions\r\n\r\nAt the minimum I'd suggest that documentation more explicitly mentions the default behavior\r\n\r\nPlease let me know what you think",
    "closed_at": "2024-03-31T11:51:11Z",
